# Echoes captured after writing SCfg (62) and RCfg (63), 2026-07-28.
#
# Both are 2 config bytes + a 100-byte DyData program, matching the declared
# 102. We wrote campfire's program so it would be recognisable coming back.
#
# THE DEVICE ECHOED 106 BYTES, not the 102 written. It appended four bytes of
# its own, "40 40 00 7e", so the declared size is the writable portion and the
# device stores more. Those four bytes are unexplained; they are identical for
# SCfg and RCfg.
#
# Key 65 RStime rode along with both writes, as it did with RiseSet, always
# reading 06 01 11 28. It is clearly tied to the sunrise/sunset family.
scfg_echo_tail: 40 40 00 7e
rcfg_echo_tail: 40 40 00 7e
rstime: 06 01 11 28
